I did some tests and it would seem to me that the C library function gmtime()
doesn't take leap seconds into account when converting from a time_t variable
to a tm structure. This is on the DEC OSF/1 3.2 machine I'm using for
development. Is this a platform-specific bug or is this function not required
by the ISO/ANSI standards to take leap seconds into account on any platform?
If it's the former, are there any Unix operating systems where gmtime() takes
leap seconds into account? If so, which ones?

And before I reinvent the wheel, does anyone have the source code to a
portable version of gmtime() that does in fact take leap seconds into
account?

Please respond by e-mail in addition to posting, if possible.

Thanks,
Ed



